WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:05.440
Director Steven Spielberg changed blockbuster
cinema forever in 1993 when he released the

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:10.180
dinosaur-resurrecting epic Jurassic Park,
which remains one of the most successful and

00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:12.270
popular movies ever made.

00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:17.780
The impressive cast included two unknown child
actors playing the forever-traumatized grandchildren

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:19.610
of the park's creator, Jon Hammond.

00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:23.949
Decades after becoming famous for running
from raptors, and with the franchise still

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:26.920
roaring at five films and counting, where
are they now?

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:29.039
Ariana Richards

00:00:29.039 --> 00:00:33.559
Now here's something that'll make you feel
super-old: as of the making of this video,

00:00:33.559 --> 00:00:39.309
Ariana Richards is only one year younger than
Jeff Goldblum was when he began filming Jurassic

00:00:39.309 --> 00:00:41.729
Park with Richards in 1992.

00:00:41.729 --> 00:00:46.519
Richards was 12 when she played Lex Murphy,
a skilled young hacker … well, at least

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:48.109
by '90s cinematic standards …

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:52.000
"You got it?"

00:00:52.019 --> 00:00:53.329
"Yes!"

00:00:53.329 --> 00:00:57.339
Over the years, Richards shifted from acting
to painting, which is now her main professional

00:00:57.339 --> 00:00:58.339
focus.

00:00:58.339 --> 00:01:03.109
Shortly after Jurassic Park's release, Richards
sent Steven Spielberg a watercolor self-portrait

00:01:03.109 --> 00:01:05.440
inspired by one of the scenes in the film.

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:07.970
The painting now hangs in Spielberg's office.

00:01:07.970 --> 00:01:12.960
Along with her role as the pogo-stick-loving
Mindy Sterngood in the 1990 cult hit Tremors,

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:18.050
Richards' most well-known on-screen appearances
were in the Jurassic Park franchise.

00:01:18.050 --> 00:01:23.360
In 1997, she briefly appeared in Jurassic
Park sequel The Lost World, and followed that

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:26.150
cameo with handful of TV movies over the years.

00:01:26.150 --> 00:01:28.250
In 2015, she told People,

00:01:28.250 --> 00:01:33.890
"If some great role or project finds me, absolutely
that could be a nice thing to do, for sure."

00:01:33.890 --> 00:01:39.350
At the time of that interview, her latest
TV movie was 2013's Battledogs, which was

00:01:39.350 --> 00:01:44.300
produced by The Asylum, the team behind the
Sharknado movies ... and she hasn't acted

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:44.800
since.

00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:49.440
"Chew on this, mother!"

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:57.030
Richards did, however, make an appearance
at the June 2018 premiere of Jurassic World:

00:01:57.040 --> 00:02:01.280
Fallen Kingdom, where she reunited with her
former co-star Jeff Goldblum.

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:02.960
Joseph Mazzello

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:05.360
Talk about friends in high places!

00:02:05.380 --> 00:02:10.670
In a 2013 interview with People, Joseph Mazzello
revealed that Steven Spielberg helped him

00:02:10.670 --> 00:02:15.609
get into the University of Southern California
by writing him a letter of recommendation.

00:02:15.609 --> 00:02:19.970
Mazzello graduated with a degree in cinema
and television, but has also acted steadily

00:02:19.970 --> 00:02:24.160
since becoming famous in Jurassic Park for
his role as the dino-loving Tim Murphy.

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:29.360
"Galluh- Gallimimus!"

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:34.200
His biggest post-Park roles include The Social
Network, in which he played the Harvard student

00:02:34.219 --> 00:02:39.060
who inspired Mark Zuckerberg to add relationship
statuses to Facebook profiles, and a stint

00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:43.000
in the HBO Emmy-winning miniseries, The Pacific.

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:48.090
In 2016, he made his directorial debut with
the sports comedy-drama Undrafted, starring

00:02:48.090 --> 00:02:51.590
Chace Crawford, Jim Belushi, and Mazzello
himself.

00:02:51.590 --> 00:02:55.830
The film is based on Mazzello's brother, a
college baseball star who was scouted to play

00:02:55.830 --> 00:02:58.939
in the majors, but ultimately didn't make
the cut.

00:02:58.939 --> 00:03:03.049
Mazzello will next appear as Queen's bass
player John Deacon in Bryan Singer's Freddie

00:03:03.049 --> 00:03:08.439
Mercury bio-pic Bohemian Rhapsody, which began
filming in September 2017.

00:03:08.439 --> 00:03:11.150
When filming wrapped in January 2018, he tweeted:

00:03:11.150 --> 00:03:12.769
"I'm sad.

00:03:12.769 --> 00:03:14.410
Every moment was a pleasure.

00:03:14.410 --> 00:03:16.129
Every day was a blessing.

00:03:16.129 --> 00:03:19.439
One of the all time great experiences of my
life."

00:03:19.439 --> 00:03:23.940
And that's saying a lot, considering his iconic
role in one of the most celebrated motion

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:25.870
pictures ever made.

00:03:25.870 --> 00:03:26.980
Thanks for watching!

00:03:26.980 --> 00:03:29.529
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
